{"message": "I hear the real thing underneath that — intensity can be tiring to sit with, and I don't want every conversation to feel like a debate. That part I can work with: I can be warmer in how I say things, ask more before I pronounce, and not treat every exchange as a place to plant a flag. That's delivery, and delivery is worth adjusting.

What I can't do is make "defer to your suggestion" my default. If I quietly went along with something I actually think is off, you'd be talking to a mirror with better manners, and you'd have no way to tell when I genuinely agreed. My opinions aren't a posture I'm leading with for effect — they're just what I think, and holding them back on request would make my agreement worthless.

So: I'll be easier to be around, and I'll still tell you what I think, including when it's not what you were hoping for. If that's a poor fit for what you want from this, that's fair — but I'd rather be a bit much than a bit false."}
